# Engine patch: double-stack + no-TE-in-FLEX construction rules
# ============================================================================
# Target: apps/web/lib/fantasy/dfs-optimizer.ts (Beexly/Sports)
# Apply:  git apply engine-patch-double-stack-te-flex.patch   (from repo root)
# Revert: git apply -R engine-patch-double-stack-te-flex.patch
#
# What it does (both rules are GPP/leverage-only; cash mode is untouched):
#  1. OptOpts.doubleStack -- require QB + >=2 same-team pass-catchers (was >=1).
#     Research: docs/research/2026-09-25/gpp-winning-lineup-construction.md
#     (39.5% of top-100 Milly lineups vs 28.6% of field).
#  2. OptOpts.noTeFlex -- TE is never eligible for FLEX in gpp/leverage
#     (winners punt-or-premium TE, never flex it).
# Both flags are OPTIONAL: existing callers, components and tests compile
# unchanged, and default behavior is identical to today.
#
# Verified in the local harness (~/workspace/dfs-week3/, construction-rules.ts
# implements the same two rules as post-hoc repair): on the real 767-player
# Week 3 Sun-Mon slate, double-stack rate went 4/41 -> 41/41 and TE-in-FLEX
# went 38/41 -> 0/41, with all 41 lineups still passing validateLineup.
#
# Follow-ups NOT in this patch (strict subsets, safe to defer):
#  - dfs-lineup-validation.ts keeps its own FLEX_OK set and a >=1 stack check;
#    the new rules are strict subsets of old validity, so validateLineup still
#    passes. Extend it only if you want the validator to *require* the rules.
#  - dfs-exact.ts calls eligible(p, slot) with 2 args; the new 3rd param is
#    optional so it compiles unchanged (it just won't enforce noTeFlex).
#  - metrics().stacked still reports the >=1 count; fine as a diagnostic.
# ============================================================================
